"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/7dd20b952257a3355c728716113cff772f7c5185/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Cause: `to_cents` truncates floating-point error. `19.99 * 100` is `1998.9999\u2026`, which `int` turns into `1998`, and `4.35 * 100` becomes `434`.\npytest isn't installed, so I'll run the test functions directly.\nI fixed the bug in `ledger/currency.py`; all four tests in `tests/test_totals.py` now pass.\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` converted dollars to cents with `int(amount * 100)`, which chops off everything after the decimal point. Floating-point math makes `19.99 * 100` come out as `1998.999\u2026`, so it became 1998 cents instead of 1999. The same thing turned 4.35 into 434 cents, which also threw off the discount test.\n\n**Fix:** changed it to `round(amount * 100)`, which rounds to the nearest cent.\n\n**Check:** pytest isn't installed here, so I called each test function directly with `python3`. All four totals tests and the one in `tests/test_report.py` passed.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 92070, "requests_cache_write": 10415, "requests_cost_usd": 0.098441, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 1394, "rere